flf2a$ 2 2 7 -1 20 0 0 82

Commodore 64 FIGfont (phm-c64.flf) by Philippe Majerus (www.phm.lu)
This font uses Unicode 16.0 octant characters to render characters from the
Commodore 64 computer chargen (characters generator) ROM.
Note PETSCII is based on an early ASCII version and does not include all
Basic Latin characters. Notably missing are `{|¦}~, ^ uses its upwards arrow
form (↑), and \ is replaced by the pound sign (£). Also, originally the _ at
U+005F was a leftwards arrow (←), but PETSCII includes a low line at 0xA4
that This font uses instead.

Unicode 16.0 defines the horizontal and vertical one-eighth lines. While the
Commodore 64 has one-quarter lines (double thickness) instead of those,
PETSCII is based on the original Commodore PET character set that used single
thickness. This is the reason of duplicated center horizontal and center
vertical lines on the Commodore 64, as it doubled the thickness towards the
center for all those lines. So this font maps them to their one-eighth code
points, repecting the original PETSCII.

Date: January 14-16, 2025

